            <div xml:id="d642">

                <pb facs="0550" n="434" xml:id="pg434"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.124/271.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 172.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1912-12-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 20, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that Colonel
                    Gorgas, accompanied by Major Noble and Mr. McGuigan, Secretary of the
                    Commission, arrived at Quito December 15 for the purpose of paying their
                    respects to President Plaza and other members of the Government. The Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs gave a luncheon in honor of the Commission, which left for
                    Guayaquil December 18.</p>
                <p>So far the visit of the Sanitary Commission to Ecuador has been a most pleasant
                    one in every respect.</p>
                <p>I am informed that the Commission will return to Panama on the steamer sailing
                    from Guayaquil December 21.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rutherfurd Bingham.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
